{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 107,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O give thanks to the LORD, for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good; for his mercy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "endureth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the redeemed of the LORD say ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", whom he hath redeemed from the hand of the enemy;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And gathered them out of the lands, from the east, and from the west, from the north, and from the south.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They wandered in the wilderness in a solitary way; they found no city to dwell in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they cried to the LORD in their trouble, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he delivered them out of their distresses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he led them forth by the right way, that they might go to a city of habitation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would praise the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his goodness, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his wonderful works to the children of men!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he satisfieth the longing soul, and filleth the hungry soul with goodness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Such as sit in darkness and in the shades of death, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bound in affliction and iron;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because they rebelled against the words of God, and contemned the counsel of the Most High:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore he brought down their heart with labor; they fell down, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none to help.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they cried to the LORD in their trouble, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he saved them out of their distresses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He brought them out of darkness and the shades of death, and broke their bands asunder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would praise the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his goodness, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his wonderful works to the children of men!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he hath broken the gates of brass, and cut the bars of iron asunder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fools, because of their transgression, and because of their iniquities, are afflicted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their soul abhorreth all manner of food; and they draw near to the gates of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they cry to the LORD in their trouble, he saveth them out of their distresses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from their destructions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would praise the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his goodness, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his wonderful works to the children of men!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And let them sacrifice the sacrifices of thanksgiving, and declare his works with rejoicing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They that go down to the sea in ships, that do business on great waters;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These see the works of the LORD, and his wonders in the deep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he commandeth, and raiseth the stormy wind, which lifteth up its waves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They mount up to the heaven, they go down again to the depths: their soul is melted because of trouble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They reel to and fro, and stagger like a drunken man, and are at their wit's end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they cry to the LORD in their trouble, and he bringeth them out of their distresses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He maketh the storm a calm, so that the waves ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the sea",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are still.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then are they glad because they are quiet; so he bringeth them to their desired haven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " would praise the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his goodness, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his wonderful works to the children of men!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them exalt him also in the congregation of the people, and praise him in the assembly of the elders.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He turneth rivers into a wilderness, and the water-springs into dry ground;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fruitful land into barrenness, for the wickedness of them that dwell in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He turneth the wilderness into a standing water, and dry ground into water-springs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there he maketh the hungry to dwell, that they may prepare a city for habitation;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And sow the fields, and plant vineyards, which may yield fruits of increase.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He blesseth them also, so that they are multiplied greatly; and suffereth not their cattle to decrease.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Again, they are diminished and brought low through oppression, affliction, and sorrow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He poureth contempt upon princes, and causeth them to wander in the wilderness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "where there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet he setteth the poor on high from affliction, and maketh him families like a flock.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The righteous shall see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and rejoice: and all iniquity shall stop her mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.107.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.107.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wise, and will observe these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", even they shall understand the loving-kindness of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
